00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:09.110 align:start position:0%
 
have it your way  harry potter is one of the most beloved  book and film series ever made but did  you know that one of the series films  almost didn't make the cut  from directors leaving to political  issues to exceeding the film's budget  and even lead actors contemplating  quitting altogether the fifth  installment of the harry potter  franchise almost didn't happen  harry potter and the order of the  phoenix had a lot of issues during  production starting with its initial  development before directors were even  selected several of the film's leading  actors were considering quitting rupert  grant who played harry's best friend ron  weasley apparently considered leaving  the harry potter franchise wondering  what life would look like if he called  it a day emma watson who played the  third member of the harry potter trio  hermione considered pulling out as well  saying i think i was scared i felt like  i got to a tipping point where i was  like this is kind of forever now she  explained that she felt lonely during  the whole ordeal saying the fame thing  had really hit home in a big way after  the release of the fourth film the  goblet of fire although they considered  leaving the wizarding world of harry  potter both grit and watson ultimately  decided to stay on for the rest of the  series this wasn't the only issue though  the film also had some trouble  attracting serious talent the goblet of  fire director mike newell turned down an  offer to return for the film as well as  jean-pierre janu matthew vaughn mira  nair and guillermo del toro one of the  most creative fantasy writers and  directors of all time this inability to  find a director along with the leading  cast members considering dropping out  almost led to the end of the movie  franchise as we know it however they  were eventually able to find a director  instead of getting a talented and bold  director though the production team  settled on david yates and in my opinion  david yates is a pretty boring director  rather than focusing on the theme of  unity in the face of evil as it was in  the book yates changed the focus of the  film to teen rebellion and the abusive  power he made a very political movie  rather than a continuation of the  character's stories from the goblet of  fire then another issue came up with the  film steve cloves the screenwriter of  the first four harry potter films  decided to not return for the order of  the phoenix instead the team settled on  michael goldenberg as screenwriter who  helped to write the script for 2011's  the green lantern one of the most  infamously bad superhero movies of all  time also john williams famous for his  work on films such as indiana jones star  wars and jurassic park did not return to  score the film instead being replaced by  nicholas hooper the problems didn't stop  there though the casting directors held  a casting call of over 15 000 young  women standing in a line that stretched  over a mile long before finally settling  on ivana lynch for the role of luna  lovegood the team had other casting  issues as well helen mccrory was  initially announced to be playing the  role of bellatrix lestrange but then had  to back out because she revealed that  she was three months pregnant and would  be unable to perform the intense battle  sequences in the ministry of magic they  then re-cast the role to helena bonham  carter which was a great decision and  mccrory was later cast as narcissa  malfoy for the next film one of the  biggest issues the film faced was its  ever increasing budget the film's sets  were some of the most costly and  extravagant out of the entire franchise  the set for the atrium in the ministry  of magic was over 200 feet in length  making it the largest and most expensive  set ever built for the harry potter  series additionally the set in the hall  of prophecies was built entirely  digitally which was very costly to do at  the time filming was also paused several  times so daniel radcliffe and emma  watson could complete their high school  exams which further raised the budget by  the end of filming though they had shot  a hyper expensive 3 hour plus long movie  which was cut down quite a lot to its  final 2 hour and 18 minute run time the  film's budget was reportedly between 150  and 200 million dollars surpassing the  previously largest budget of the other  films in the series in total it was  estimated that the film made around 942  million dollars worldwide making it the  second highest grossing film of 2007  just behind pirates of the caribbean at  world's end it was assumed that warner  bros made a pretty good profit on the  movie but that wasn't the case according  to leaked financial documents the studio  reported a loss of over 167 million  dollars on the film so while the order  of the phoenix adaptation ultimately was  made it seems as if it shouldn't have at  least financially and because of all the  trouble it took to make it happen  although the order of the phoenix was  pretty successful at the box office it  almost wasn't made and without it we  wouldn't have this  you may not like it minister  but you can't deny  dumbledore got style  anyways that's gonna be all for today if  you like what you saw maybe check out  the video on your screen for some  different content i make videos on  basically anything that interests me in  the world of entertainment also don't  forget to like and subscribe as it truly  does help me out and thanks for watching  rocket riley

